<mxCell id="__frame" value="" style="rounded=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="1800" height="860" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="pfw" value="VM-Series&lt;br&gt;one-arm on ethernet1/2" style="shape=mxgraph.networks.firewall;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#FA582D;outlineConnect=0;verticalLabelPosition=middle;verticalAlign=middle;labelPosition=right;align=left;spacingLeft=4;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=15;fontColor=#201F1E;labelBackgroundColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="60" width="80" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="cfg" value="&lt;b&gt;Minimum PAN-OS configuration&lt;/b&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:950px;font-size:17px;margin-top:6px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;background:#E1DFDD;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Item&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;background:#E1DFDD;width:72%;&quot;&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Zones&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;ethernet1/1 untrust, ethernet1/2 trust&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Static route&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;10.0.0.0/8 → 10.0.2.1 out ethernet1/2 (all spokes and endpoints)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Probe route + profile&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;168.63.129.16/32 → 10.0.2.1; mgmt profile allows HTTPS from it&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Security rule&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;trust → trust, app-subnets → pe-subnets, ssl + web-browsing, log at end&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;intrazone-default&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;override to &lt;b&gt;deny&lt;/b&gt; and log (spoke traffic is trust → trust)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Source NAT&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;trust → trust to pe-subnets, dynamic IP and port, interface ethernet1/2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:28%;&quot;&gt;Optional&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:72%;&quot;&gt;custom URL category with your account and vault FQDNs (TLS SNI)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=20;fontColor=#201F1E;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8A8886;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="190" width="1000" height="650" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="why" value="&lt;b&gt;Why it looks like this&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Traffic enters through the ILB on ethernet1/2 and leaves on ethernet1/2 toward the endpoint, so the firewall sees &lt;b&gt;trust → trust&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;PAN-OS allows intrazone traffic by default. Without the override, any spoke could reach any endpoint, and nothing gets logged.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SNAT keeps the reply on the same firewall behind the load balancer, and makes the NSG on snet-pe meaningful.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With two firewalls, keep the ILB&#x27;s HA ports rule. Each flow sticks to one firewall in both directions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The full set of commands is in &lt;b&gt;panos/fw-config.set&lt;/b&gt; in the lab." style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=20;fontColor=#201F1E;fillColor=#E9F6EC;strokeColor=#107C10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1050" y="40" width="730" height="800" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
<diagram name="guard"><mxGraphModel dx="0" dy="0" grid="0" page="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
<mxCell id="__frame" value="" style="rounded=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="1800" height="860" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="g1" value="&lt;b&gt;Lock it so it can&#x27;t drift&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• NSG on every snet-pe: allow 443 from the firewall SNAT IPs, deny VirtualNetwork&lt;br&gt;• Azure Policy: deny PE subnets without network policies, deny public network access&lt;br&gt;• Every client subnet gets the spoke route table, including &lt;b&gt;App Service and Functions VNet integration subnets&lt;/b&gt; (with all outbound traffic routed into the VNet)&lt;br&gt;• Virtual Network Manager routing configurations can push the same route tables to every spoke" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=20;fontColor=#201F1E;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8A8886;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="870" height="400" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="g2" value="&lt;b&gt;DNS doesn&#x27;t change the path, but it must resolve privately&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• privatelink.blob.core.windows.net and privatelink.vaultcore.azure.net live once, centrally&lt;br&gt;• Link them to the hub (resolver) or to every spoke&lt;br&gt;• Spokes use Azure DNS or the resolver; on-premises forwards to the resolver inbound IP&lt;br&gt;• Point the firewall&#x27;s DNS at the resolver too, so FQDN objects match private IPs" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=20;fontColor=#201F1E;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8A8886;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="910" y="20" width="870" height="400" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="g3" value="&lt;b&gt;Other layouts, if you can change where endpoints live&lt;/b&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:1700px;font-size:17px;margin-top:6px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;background:#E1DFDD;width:30%;&quot;&gt;Layout&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;background:#E1DFDD;width:36%;&quot;&gt;Routes you maintain&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;background:#E1DFDD;width:34%;&quot;&gt;Trade-off&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:30%;&quot;&gt;Endpoints in each spoke (this lecture)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:36%;&quot;&gt;one PE-subnet route per spoke + one per remote spoke&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:34%;&quot;&gt;teams own their endpoints; more route tables&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:30%;&quot;&gt;Dedicated private endpoint spoke&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:36%;&quot;&gt;one route for its address space&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:34%;&quot;&gt;Microsoft&#x27;s most scalable pattern; central team owns endpoints&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:30%;&quot;&gt;Virtual WAN with routing intent&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:36%;&quot;&gt;none by hand: the hub NVA or Cloud NGFW attracts private traffic&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #A19F9D;padding:4px 6px;text-align:left;width:34%;&quot;&gt;needs a supported NVA in the virtual hub&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=20;fontColor=#201F1E;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8A8886;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="450" width="1760" height="390" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
